# Custom Network Config Reference

The files `config_hpcc_case*.txt` are ns-3 base configs consumed by
`extern/network_backend/ns-3/scratch/common.h`. The custom input generator
rewrites path and selected runtime keys into `generated/<scenario>/network_config.txt`.

## Required Path Keys

- `TOPOLOGY_FILE`: generated physical topology file.
- `FLOW_FILE`: generated flow override file.
- `TRACE_FILE`: generated trace-node file.
- `TRACE_OUTPUT_FILE`, `FCT_OUTPUT_FILE`, `PFC_OUTPUT_FILE`, `QLEN_MON_FILE`: ns-3 output paths.

## Forwarding Keys

- `DEFAULT_FWD_MODE`: default per-flow forwarding mode. `0` means flow ECMP, `1` means packet spray. A flow row can override this through its `strategy` value.
- `FLOW_STRATEGY`: flow-based routing strategy. Currently `0` is ECMP.
- `PACKET_STRATEGY`: packet-spray routing strategy. With `ENABLE_ARN 0`, currently only `0` is round-robin. With `ENABLE_ARN 1`, `2` enables HPCC-style DLB.
- `ARN_PACKET_STRATEGY`: backward-compatible ARN strategy field; `PACKET_STRATEGY` is authoritative for ARN packet-spray selection.
- `ENABLE_ARN`: ARN feature switch. `0` disables ARN generation and uses ARN-off packet spray. `1` enables ARN notification handling and ARN packet-spray strategies.
- `ARN_INTERVAL`: minimum interval in ns between repeated ARN notifications for the same path.
- `ARN_CONGESTION_QLEN`: egress queue length threshold in bytes used to trigger ARN. The clear threshold is `7/8 * ARN_CONGESTION_QLEN`.
- `Q_LEVEL`: ascending queue-length thresholds used to discretize local queue quality.
- `LOAD_LEVEL`: ascending byte-per-second thresholds used to discretize HPCC `calcBandwidth` quality.

When ARN is enabled, `PACKET_STRATEGY` follows HPCC ARN numbering: `0=ARN_SCALE`, `1=ARN_REJECT`, `2=DLB`, `3=GLB`. This branch implements DLB first.

## ARN-Aware Selection

When ARN is enabled, congested leaf or spine switches emit ARN packets for packet-spray data traffic. With `PACKET_STRATEGY 2`, DLB chooses the lowest local `q_level + load_level` among equal-cost next hops and randomly breaks ties.

## Example

```text
FLOW_STRATEGY 0
PACKET_STRATEGY 0
ARN_PACKET_STRATEGY 0
DEFAULT_FWD_MODE 1
ENABLE_ARN 1
ARN_INTERVAL 10000
ARN_CONGESTION_QLEN 5000000
Q_LEVEL 2 0 5000000
LOAD_LEVEL 2 0 50000000000
```

## Queue And ECN Keys

- `KMIN_MAP`, `KMAX_MAP`, `PMAX_MAP`: per-link-rate ECN thresholds. Every link bandwidth in the topology must have entries.
- `BUFFER_SIZE`: switch buffer size in MB.
- `HEADROOM_FACTOR`: multiplier for PFC headroom calculation.
- `QLEN_MON_START`, `QLEN_MON_END`, `QLEN_MON_INTERVAL`: queue monitor window and period in ns.
